Subject: Skip exporting an empty stroke border

ft_stroke_border_export() memcpy()s border->points even when the border
has no points, and an empty border's point array is NULL: passing NULL to
memcpy() is undefined behaviour even with a zero length (UBSan
nonnull-attribute). A polygon whose points list breaks off after one
point, stroked, reaches it -- found by zusvg's fuzzer. There is nothing to
export, so return first.

zusvg: .agents/design.md §9. Offered upstream.

--- a/plutovg/source/plutovg-ft-stroker.c
+++ b/plutovg/source/plutovg-ft-stroker.c
@@ -568,6 +568,8 @@
                                     PVG_FT_Outline*     outline)
 {
     /* copy point locations */
+    if (border->num_points == 0)
+        return;
     memcpy(outline->points + outline->n_points, border->points,
            border->num_points * sizeof(PVG_FT_Vector));
 
